# GHDL Simulation Environment

## Overview

This directory contains the GHDL simulation environment for the DexterLab Command Parser.

It provides a standalone testbench environment for validating the parser together with the reference slave models and supported bus converters using GHDL and GTKWave.

This README focuses only on how to run simulations.

For parser architecture, command format, response format, and bus-converter behavior, please refer to the main project documentation.

---

## Directory Structure

| File / Directory | Description |
|------------------|-------------|
| Makefile | Automation for compile, elaborate, simulate and waveform viewing |
| cmd.txt | Command sequence executed by the parser regression tests |
| ram_init.cde | Initial RAM contents used by the reference slave |
| workdir/ | GHDL working directory (object files and elaboration artifacts) |
| wave.ghw / wave.vcd / wave.fst | Generated waveform files |
| README.md | This document |

---

## Requirements

- GHDL (LLVM or mcode backend recommended)
- GTKWave (for waveform visualization)
- MSYS2 / MINGW64 or Linux shell environment
- Standard VHDL-93 support

---

## Makefile Overview

The Makefile supports:

- Multiple VHDL standards (93, 93c, 2002, 2008)
- Selectable waveform formats (ghw, vcd, fst)
- Separate compilation of RTL and testbench sources
- Elaboration of the top-level testbench
- Batch simulation
- Interactive waveform viewing

The default top-level entity is:

```text
tb_parser
```

The default waveform format is:

```text
ghw
```

---

## Running the Simulation

### Full Simulation (Compile + Elaborate + Run)

```sh
make all
```

This performs:

- Cleanup
- RTL compilation
- Testbench compilation
- Elaboration
- Simulation execution

Waveform output is generated according to the selected waveform format.

---

### Batch Simulation Only

```sh
make sim
```

Runs the testbench with a command similar to:

```sh
ghdl -r tb_parser --wave=wave.ghw --stop-time=200us
```

The stop time can be adjusted in the Makefile.

---

### Interactive Simulation + Waveform Viewer

```sh
make simwave
```

This target:

- Removes any previous waveform
- Runs the simulation with `--assert-level=note`
- Opens GTKWave automatically

Useful during debugging and validation.

---

## Waveform Viewing

Open GTKWave manually:

```sh
make wave
```

or

```sh
gtkwave wave.ghw &
```

---

## Debug Logging

Debug messages (`severity note`) are controlled by:

```vhdl
constant ENABLE_DEBUG_LOG : boolean := false;
```

Defined in:

```text
cmd_cfg.vhd
```

### Debug OFF (Default)

- Suppresses debug messages
- Keeps warning, error and fatal messages enabled

### Debug ON

Set:

```vhdl
ENABLE_DEBUG_LOG := true;
```

Although GHDL supports severity filtering through `--assert-level`, the recommended approach is to control debug output directly from the VHDL configuration.

---

## Cleaning the Directory

To remove generated files:

```sh
make clean
```

This removes:

- `workdir/*.o`
- `workdir/*.cf`
- Generated waveform files
- Local object and compilation artifacts

---

## Supported Verification Targets

The simulation environment is used to validate:

- Core parser functionality
- Command decoding
- Response generation
- WAIT / POLL / PING / DUMP mechanisms
- SINGLE command execution
- BURST command execution
- FIFO command execution
- WRAP address handling
- Timeout detection
- Error handling and reporting
- AXI-Full bus converter
- AXI-Lite bus converter
- AHB-Full bus converter
- AHB-Lite bus converter

